{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logger", "label": "Logger-Interface", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Calls below the configured level emit nothing, but the arguments are ordinary function arguments and are evaluated first \u2014 expensive payloads need a manual level guard.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_displayname", "label": "displayName()", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A path is an address, not a name, and grows unreadable under sharding; the display name is added beside source, is resolved per record so it can follow state and restarts, and stays a human label \u2014 never an identity.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_jsonlogger", "label": "JsonLogger", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "One newline-terminated JSON object per record for aggregator pipelines; Errors serialize to name/message/stack because their enumerable surface is empty, and cycles, BigInt and functions are sanitized so a log call never throws.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_otellogger", "label": "otelLogger (OTLP-Logs-Pipeline)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "@opentelemetry/api-logs stays an optional peer the framework never imports \u2014 the caller brings its existing namespace import.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_withfields", "label": "withFields (statische Felder)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Bind it in preStart, not in a field initializer: this.context only exists once the actor is attached.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logcontext", "label": "LogContext (MDC)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Backed by AsyncLocalStorage; values are restricted to string/number/boolean because the context serializes to JSON across cluster hops and arbitrary objects do not round-trip.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logcontext_runfresh", "label": "LogContext.runFresh", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The inverse of with(): starting empty fails safe, because a field nobody set cannot leak, and is easier to audit than remembering which keys to strip.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logcontext_runeach", "label": "LogContext.runEach", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Returns Promise<void> on purpose \u2014 ordering and one scope per item are the product, not results; an error propagates immediately because swallowing it would be a supervision decision inside a diagnostic primitive.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logcontextentry", "label": "LogContextEntry", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Exported precisely because a queue outlives the round that filled it, so the field holding snapshotted context needs a type.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_mdc_propagation", "label": "MDC-Propagation \u00fcber tell und Cluster-Hops", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The runtime snapshots the current context onto the envelope and the receiver runs onReceive under a fresh run of that snapshot, so one correlationId spans a multi-actor, multi-node request.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_deferred_work_tenant_leak", "label": "Aufgeschobene Arbeit und Tenant-Isolation", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "AsyncLocalStorage binds the store when the async resource is created, so work that outlives its round inherits that round's context \u2014 a data leak across tenants, not just a confusing log line.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_level_guard", "label": "Level-Guard f\u00fcr teure Payloads", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Arguments to a log call are ordinary function arguments and are evaluated before the level check, so an expensive snapshot runs even at info level and its result is thrown away \u2014 wrap it in an explicit level guard.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_multi_sink_logging", "label": "Multi-Sink-Logging", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_displayname", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logger", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_jsonlogger", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logger", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_otellogger", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logger", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_withfields", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logger", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logcontext", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_withfields", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/logging.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_logging_logcon